<DocsLayout title="Connecting an agent">
  <p>
    Any MCP-compatible agent — Claude Code, Claude Desktop, or a custom tool — can connect
    directly to a drain: reading it for context before starting work, and writing its own entries
    as it goes. Agent-written entries are attributed <code>via &lt;token name&gt;</code> and appear
    in the same timeline as everything else, never a separate audit log.
  </p>

  <h2>Add the server</h2>
  <p>Add this to your MCP client's config — Claude Desktop's <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code>, or Claude Code's <code>.claude/settings.json</code> under <code>mcpServers</code>:</p>

  <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "drains": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "github:drains-dev/mcp"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

  <p>No install step — <code>npx</code> fetches it from GitHub on first run.</p>

  <h2>Get a token</h2>
  <p>
    Open a drain, click your avatar in the sidebar → <strong>API tokens</strong> → create one.
    Tokens are scoped to your account (not a single drain) and can be revoked at any time from the
    same menu — see <a href="/docs/api">API tokens</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What an agent can do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read and search entries in any drain the token's account can access</li>
    <li>Create new entries — <code>@mentions</code> and <code>[[ references ]]</code> are parsed the same way they are for a human-typed entry</li>
    <li>List and manage drain members</li>
    <li>Update drain metadata (title, description, tags)</li>
  </ul>

  <p>See <a href="/AGENTS.md">AGENTS.md</a> for the full machine-readable version of this page.</p>
</DocsLayout>
